.\" kubectl-kwd(1) - kwd as a kubectl plugin
.\" Manual page for kubectl-kwd
.TH KUBECTL\-KWD 1 "2026-10-09" "kwd v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kubectl\-kwd \- run kwd as a kubectl plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kubectl kwd
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kubectl\-kwd
is the
.B kwd
CLI packaged under the
.I kubectl-
prefix so kubectl plugin discovery resolves it as
.BR "kubectl kwd" .
It is the same binary and accepts the same commands and flags; see
.BR kwd (1)
for the full manual.
.PP
Flag parity with
.BR kwd (1)
includes
.B check \-\-interval
(seconds;
.B 0
= single-pass; YAML →
.B KWD_INTERVAL
→ flag),
.B \-\-listen
(YAML →
.B KWD_HTTP_LISTEN
→ flag),
.BR \-\-confirm\-alert ,
.BR \-\-confirm\-ok ,
and
.BR \-\-repeat\-while\-firing
(each applies only when set). There is no
.B \-\-daemon
flag.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kwd (1),
.BR kubectl (1)
.PP
